  "reason": "The current best is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688 acc. The image-only resnet50 baseline was very weak (0.208), suggesting the image modality's contribution in the multimodal model may be limited by the encoder quality. Config_038 isolates the image encoder effect by replacing resnet50 with imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other settings identical to the best config (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, concat). This is a single-variable change from the current best, making it a clean test. If ViT-L substantially improves the image component, it could yield a meaningful accuracy gain and open a productive direction for the remaining 2 experiments (e.g., testing weighted fusion with ViT-L). If it does not, it confirms the image modality is inherently limited here, redirecting effort toward RNA-side refinements. This high-information experiment is the best use of slot 8 given the uncertainty about whether a stronger image encoder can unlock more multimodal benefit."
